  "worked_solution": "First, let's find the measures of unknown angles. Since the sum of the measures of internal angles of a quadrilateral is ${360}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A+m∠B+m∠C+m∠D & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ {68}^{∘}+m∠B+{85}^{∘}+{111}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ m∠B+{264}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ m∠B & ={96}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠M+m∠N+m∠K+m∠L & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ {68}^{∘}+{96}^{∘}+m∠K+{111}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ m∠K+{275}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ m∠K & ={85}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the quadrilaterals are similar, and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∠A≅∠M,\\,∠B≅∠N,\\,∠C≅∠K,\\,∠D≅∠L.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that \n\n- $A$ corresponds to $M,$\n\n- $B$ corresponds to $N,$\n\n- $C$ corresponds to $K,$\n\n- $D$ corresponds to $L.$\n\nTherefore, $ABCD∼MNKL.$",
